{"document_id": "65eea35f-4e3d-4b46-93a2-e4ef47602c46", "crop": "mango", "organization": "Unknown", "source": "Unknown", "source_url": "https://mango-crop.web.app/diseasemanage/dismgtstemendrot.htm", "title": "Mango - Solutions for crop management", "retrieved_at": "2026-09-06T23:42:59.115635", "content": "  * [Skip navigation](https://mango-crop.web.app/diseasemanage/dismgtstemendrot.htm#content)\n  * [Home](https://mango-crop.web.app/index.html)\n\n\n# ![](https://mango-crop.web.app/diseasemanage/imgs/dismgtpmhdr.jpg)\n[Home](https://mango-crop.web.app/) > [Previous Page](https://mango-crop.web.app/diseasemanage/dismgtstemendrot.htm#) > Current\n##  Disease management module**:: Fungal- Stem end rot**\n### Bacterial & Other Diseases\n**Bacterial Diseases** : They can cause a variety of symptoms including cankers, leaf spots, overgrowths, scabs, wilts, and others\n  * ![cancker](https://mango-crop.web.app/diseasemanage/canker1s.jpg)\n  * ![Other](https://mango-crop.web.app/diseasemanage/redrusts.jpg)\n\n\n**Others:** This disease attack can causes reduction in photosynthetic activity and defoliation of leaves thereby reducing the vitality of the host plant.\n### Fungal Diseases - Stem end rot\n_**Botryodiplodia theobromae**_\n**The fungus also causes die-back symptoms**\n**Recorded in all mango growing areas in India**\n#### Stem end rot infection on mango\n  * [ ![STem end rot\\(thumbnail\\)](https://mango-crop.web.app/diseasemanage/anthra1/stemrot1as.jpg)](https://mango-crop.web.app/diseasemanage/anthra1/stemrot1a.jpg)![ Disease \\(larger image\\)](https://mango-crop.web.app/diseasemanage/anthra1/stemrot1a.jpg) Symptoms and control !   \n**Stem end rot** It attacks the fruits. Dark epicarp is seen around the base of the pedicel at first. Affected area enlarges to form a circular, black patch.\n  * [ ![Stem end rot \\(thumbnail\\)](https://mango-crop.web.app/diseasemanage/anthra1/stemrot2as.jpg)](https://mango-crop.web.app/diseasemanage/anthra1/stemrot2a.jpg)![ Disease \\(larger image\\)](https://mango-crop.web.app/diseasemanage/anthra1/stemrot2a.jpg) Symptoms and control !   \n**Stem end rot** It attacks the fruits. Epicarp turns dark around the base of the pedicel in the initial stage. Subsequently the affected area enlarges to form a circular black patch which extends rapidly under humid atmosphere and turns the whole fruit completely black within two or three days \n\n\n  * [ ![STem end rot\\(thumbnail\\)](https://mango-crop.web.app/diseasemanage/anthra1/stemendrot3s.jpg)](https://mango-crop.web.app/diseasemanage/anthra1/stemendrot3.jpg)![ Disease \\(larger image\\)](https://mango-crop.web.app/diseasemanage/anthra1/stemendrot3.jpg) Symptoms and control !   \n**Stem end rot** The whole fruit turns black with in 3-4 days under humid environment\n  * [ ![Stem end rot \\(thumbnail\\)](https://mango-crop.web.app/diseasemanage/anthra1/stemendrot4s.jpg)](https://mango-crop.web.app/diseasemanage/anthra1/stemendrot4.jpg)![ Disease \\(larger image\\)](https://mango-crop.web.app/diseasemanage/anthra1/stemendrot4.jpg) Symptoms and control !   \n**Stem end rot** The pulp of the diseased fruits becomes brown and somewhat soft. \n\n\n( Move mouse over a thumbnail for a full sized version)\n**Stem end rot :** It attacks the fruits. Epicarp turns dark around the base of the pedicel in the initial stage. Subsequently the affected area enlarges to form a circular black patch which extends rapidly under humid atmosphere and turns the whole fruit completely black within two or three days. The pulp of the diseased fruits becomes brown and somewhat soft. Careful harvesting and subsequent handling of the fruits to avoid any injury is very important. \n  * [Home ](https://mango-crop.web.app/index.html)\n  * [Technologies](https://mango-crop.web.app/Technologies.html)\n  * [Varieties ](https://mango-crop.web.app/var/varieties.html)\n  * [Crop production](https://mango-crop.web.app/diseasemanage/dismgtstemendrot.htm#)\n  * [Crop Protection](https://mango-crop.web.app/cropprotect.html)\n  * [Crop improvement](https://mango-crop.web.app/cropimprove.html)\n  * [Machineries](https://mango-crop.web.app/Technologies/machineries.html)\n  * [Contact us](https://mango-crop.web.app/ContactUs.html)\n  * Pest management\n\n\n[ ](http://www.w3.org/html/logo/#the-logo)Mango crop managemnt and Diagnostic system::Developed by MK CHANDRA PRAKASH & REENA ROSY THOMAS\n", "html": "<!DOCTYPE html><html lang=\"en\"><head>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<title>Mango - Solutions for crop management</title>\n<meta name=\"description\" content=\"enter a brief description of your website here\">\n<meta name=\"keywords\" content=\"enter, some, keywords, seperated by, commas\">\n\n<!--STYLESHEETS-->\n<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"assets/style.css\" type=\"text/css\" media=\"screen\">\n<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"assets/print.css\" type=\"text/css\" media=\"print\">\n<!--INTERNET EXPLORER SPECIFIC STYLESHEETS-->\n<!--[if lte IE 8]>\n<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"assets/ie8_hacks.css\" type=\"text/css\" media=\"screen\" />\n<![endif]-->\n\n<!--Hekp IE8 and earlier with HTML5-->\n<!--[if lt IE 9]>\n<script src=\"http://html5shiv.googlecode.com/svn/trunk/html5.js\"></script>\n<![endif]-->\n\n<!--GOOGLE WEB FONTS USED IN THIS TEMPLATE - http://www.google.com/webfonts-->\n<link href=\"http://fonts.googleapis.com/css?family=Happy+Monkey\" rel=\"stylesheet\" type=\"text/css\">\n<style type=\"text/css\">\n.auto-style1 {\n\ttext-align: justify;\n}\n.auto-style2 {\n\tcolor: #0C460C;\n}\n.auto-style3 {\n\tfont-family: Cambria, Cochin, Georgia, Times, \"Times New Roman\", serif;\n\tfont-size: x-large;\n}\n.auto-style4 {\n\tfont-family: Tahoma;\n\ttext-align: justify;\n\tline-height: 150%;\n}\n.auto-style5 {\n\tfont-size: small;\n}\n.auto-style7 {\n\tcolor: #0C460C;\n\tfont-family: Tahoma;\n}\n.auto-style8 {\n\tfont-family: Tahoma;\n}\n.auto-style9 {\n\ttext-align: justify;\n\tfont-size: small;\n}\n.auto-style10 {\n\tmargin-left: 40px;\n}\n.auto-